{"name":"Spiced Hot Chocolate","hex":"#53433e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spiced","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having spice added, spicy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of spice"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiced"},{"term":"hot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Hote."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to heat and conditions which produce it.\n Having or giving off a high temperature.","Having or giving off a high temperature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot"},{"term":"chocolate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made from ground roasted cocoa beans.","A drink made by dissolving this food in boiling milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or containing chocolate.","Having a dark reddish-brown colour/color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Chocolate are a British soul band formed by Errol Brown and Tony Wilson. The group had at least one hit song every year on the UK Singles Chart from 1970 to 1984."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/The_Hot_Chocolate.jpg/330px-The_Hot_Chocolate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Chocolate","wikidata":"Q1368881"},{"title":"Hot chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Hot chocolate, also known as hot cocoa or drinking chocolate, is a heated drink consisting of shaved or melted chocolate or cocoa powder, and heated milk or water. It usually contains a sweetener, such as sugar, and is often garnished with whipped cream or marshmallows. Hot chocolate made with melted chocolate is characterized by less sweetness and a thicker consistency."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/After_The_St._Patrick%27s_Parade_Late_Lunch_%40_Lemon%2C_Dawson_Street%2C_Dublin%2C_Rep._Of_Ireland_A_Fine_Tradition%21_%286992614913%29.jpg/330px-After_The_St._Patrick%27s_Parade_Late_Lunch_%40_Lemon%2C_Dawson_Street%2C_Dublin%2C_Rep._Of_Ireland_A_Fine_Tradition%21_%286992614913%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_chocolate","wikidata":"Q13261"},{"title":"Spice","blocks":[{"text":"In the culinary arts, a spice is a seed, fruit, root, bark, or other plant substance primarily used for flavouring or colouring food. Spices are distinguished from herbs, which are the leaves, flowers, or stems of plants used for flavouring or as a garnish. Spices and herbs are both seasonings. \nSpices are sometimes used in medicine, religious rituals, cosmetics, or perfume production. They are usually classified into spices, spice seeds, and herbal categories. For example, vanilla is commonly used as an ingredient in fragrance manufacturing. Plant-based sweeteners such as sugar are not considered spices."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Spices1.jpg/330px-Spices1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spice","wikidata":"Q42527"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate","wikidata":"Q195"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/1998_hot_chocolate_cologne.jpg/500px-1998_hot_chocolate_cologne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe